body: |-
  ## The arc, in one line
  Conductor becomes the hybrid macOS desktop app that is the unified window for the Claude Code fleet: a custom conversation UI (structured headless stream, not terminal-scraping) + native control actions + the container for the settled presence/page/reply on-call contract.

  ## How we got here (understand-and-correlate, two rounds)
  Round 1 — correlated a-aloud's voice-comms broker (sibling repo, gitignored docs .voice-comms-architecture.md + .comms-redesign-spec.md) with Paradigm's Symphony relay. Founder forks settled: demand is real ("I live in this loop"), revive Conductor, voice = one swappable client.

  Round 2 — team dug into PewDiePie's Odysseus (/tmp/odysseus, a self-hosted AI workspace). Unanimous correction: Odysseus does not host Claude Code; its 'desktop app' is a bash launcher opening chrome --app. Founder clarified: he loved the agent-COMMUNICATION interface, and his real friction is the conversation experience with CC sessions in Conductor today. Target locked: structured headless stream + custom chat UI + custom handling, preserving the actions he's used to.

  Feasibility gate — claude-code-guide verified against docs: structured headless stream + custom UI + full action control + N concurrent sessions embedded in a macOS app is feasible TODAY. Recommended mechanism: spawn `claude` CLI with stream-json over pipes (lighter than a Node/Python SDK sidecar for a Swift app).

  ## Panel (agentIds for continuation)
  architect a0ccb00b60e31f95d; swift a6510cdb24c63e6ff; North a491b6fc3a00d62a6; Loid abf2d684f3a37c08c; Jinx a18fe7023c5df7592; claude-code-guide ac11a08c123007142. (Round-1 panel: architect a76fa5412b79ee712, swift a4b3726631546cf44, North ac18b7e36a80db460, Loid ae683732ad04e5c35, Jinx a0a4c8334fe5a0f55.)

  ## Next phase
  PLANNING (not yet started) — turn these understandings into a phased plan. Open design seams for planning: the native↔web bridge protocol (Arky owns); run abstraction + parallel-session supervision lifting Odysseus's Semaphore(1); fleet identity by archetype×project; routing all run/consult signals to ~/.paradigm/ substrate.
